  }))), "Errors and limitations of the LLM"), mdx("p", null, mdx("em", {
    parentName: "p"
  }, "Where did it fall short or make mistakes?")), mdx("p", null, "An obvious mistake is that when asked about competing approaches, SmolLM \"thought\" that the authors were suddenly competing with other models for linguistic speed and accuracy when analyzing dialects of Javanese.  However, this is not what that table was about at all.  Instead, they were comparing how the different dialects were recognized successfully or not to different degrees of success.  What is particularly interesting is that the AI ", mdx("em", {
    parentName: "p"
  }, "correctly"), " cited this table earlier on, but then used that same table to hallucinate an incorrect answer later down the line."), mdx("p", null, "Overall, SmolLM did a solid job summarizing the data, and usually did so accurately.  However, the example above was stated just as confidently as everything else, and was completely off-base.  Furthermore, while the AI was able to cite data, it only pulled from specific elements of the paper, usually tables.  It seems to have not pulled information from the graphs/images.  I am not sure if that is a SmolLM limitation or a limitation of me using the HuggingChat API, but it is worth noting all the same."), mdx("p", null, "I also found the AI to initially overemphasize the technological issues separating the underresourced languages in Indonesia at the expense of the societal/cultural issues (mentioning GPU shortages as one of the key issues), although as more questions were asked that changed quickly.  It did eventually balance out its reasoning behind the struggles of underresourced language groups in Indonesia to more closely match the original authors as the conversation went on.  I found it interesting that it seemed to reprioritize certain specific issues throughout the process, though."), mdx("p", null, "As I mentioned above, I was overall very impressed with the LLM, although its shortcomings are extremely notable and would not be easily noticed if I had not already familiarized myself with this paper.  (The example I noted above is also not its only mistake!)  In light of the fact that many individuals oftentimes use AI without checking what it is citing (from students in high school to the U.S. government's annual health report this year), it is concerning to know how easily we can be swept along by words that sound confident."), mdx("p", null, "It is, however, also very unsurprising.  That is why like any exciting and wonderful tool, AI must be carefully used and not relied upon as a crutch."), mdx("h4", 